 { Find the best continuation. (4-5 moves) } 1... { -KEY- } Kc4 $1 { Heading for the key battlefield: the kingside. } ( { Also good is } 1... Rg1 2. Kf4 Kc4 3. h4 Rh1 $1 4. Kg4 Kd5 5. h5 Ke5 { in similar fashion. } ) 
 ( { In contrast, } 1... Kb4 $6 2. h4 Kxa5 3. h5 Kb4 4. g6 a5 5. Kf4 { is less convincing. } ) 
2. Kf4 Kd5 $1 { In the same spirit of 'king first'. } ( { Instead, the game went } 2... Kb5 $2 3. h4 Kxa5 $2 ( { Black could still win with } 3... Rh1 4. Kg4 Kc5 5. h5 Kd6 ) 
4. h5 Rd4 5. Ke5 Rg4 $2 ( { this even loses, whereas } 5... Rh4 6. h6 Kb6 7. Kf6 a5 { was a last path to the win, since White is left with the "bad" g-pawn in the end. } ) 
6. g6 Kb4 7. Kf5 $1 Rg1 8. h6 a5 9. g7 a4 10. h7 Rxg7 11. h8=Q $11 { and White was winning. } ) 
3. Kf5 Rf1+ $1 { A good intermediate check to release White's obstruction. } 4. Kg6 Rh1 5. Kf7 Rxh3 6. g6 Rf3+ 7. Ke7 Rg3 8. Kf7 Kc5 9. g7 Kb5 10. g8=Q Rxg8 11. Kxg8 Kxa5 { Black wins. } 
